hasn't gone away.

762
00:28:23,067 --> 00:28:26,233
- [Tom] Are you as
turned off as I am?

763
00:28:27,467 --> 00:28:31,500
- [Mike] Oof, I'm having
another heart attack.

764
00:28:31,500 --> 00:28:34,700
- Y'know Doctor, I think
I will have that tea.

765
00:28:34,700 --> 00:28:36,800
- [Crow] It's always funny
when you turn down tea,

766
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:39,567
and then you decide
you want tea.

767
00:28:40,900 --> 00:28:43,833
- [Tom] Greg Norman
at the Master's.

768
00:28:43,833 --> 00:28:45,567
- [Dan] I told you there
was nothing out here.

769
00:28:45,567 --> 00:28:46,600
- [Mike] Shh, the
flowers are listening.

770
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:47,967
- [Dan] There's nothing.

771
00:28:47,967 --> 00:28:51,933
- [Ev] So why are you
carrying your gun?

772
00:28:51,933 --> 00:28:54,233
- [Dan] Aw, shut up.

773
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:57,533
♪ There is love

774
00:28:57,533 --> 00:28:59,133
♪ There is love

775
00:28:59,133 --> 00:29:01,567
- Since you've been
running the place,

776
00:29:01,567 --> 00:29:03,567
everything's gone wrong.

777
00:29:04,467 --> 00:29:06,167
- [Mike] Woop, plot hole.

778
00:29:06,167 --> 00:29:07,100
(woman screams)

779
00:29:07,100 --> 00:29:08,600
- [Mike] Got milk?

780
00:29:12,067 --> 00:29:13,300
- Now watch this.

781
00:29:13,300 --> 00:29:14,400
- [Crow] I'm gonna
put on a dashiki

782
00:29:14,400 --> 00:29:16,267
and blow your mind.

783
00:29:16,267 --> 00:29:17,100
- See?

784
00:29:19,167 --> 00:29:22,833
♪ What a lucky man he was

785
00:29:22,833 --> 00:29:24,600
- I just don't understand it.

786
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:26,333
- [Mike] The things I can
do with my spirograph.

787
00:29:26,333 --> 00:29:28,900
- Those radiation levels
are far too lethal.

788
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:31,900
Anyone anywhere near
the initial impact point

789
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:33,967
would be in great danger.

790
00:29:33,967 --> 00:29:35,233
- What would be the safest way

791
00:29:35,233 --> 00:29:38,233
to find the exact
point of impact?

792
00:29:38,233 --> 00:29:40,067
- [Crow] Have you do it.

793
00:29:40,067 --> 00:29:41,733
- Maybe we could
use a helicopter.

794
00:29:41,733 --> 00:29:43,367
- No no, that'd
be too dangerous.

795
00:29:43,367 --> 00:29:45,633
Doctor--
- He's got a hatchet wound!

796
00:29:45,633 --> 00:29:48,333
- We have already lost
one airplane crew.

797
00:29:48,333 --> 00:29:49,600
- I didn't know that.

798
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:52,633
- [Crow] 30 lashes
with a wet noodle.

799
00:29:54,367 --> 00:29:56,033
- Well--
- Well, back to the tea.

800
00:29:56,033 --> 00:29:58,833
- [Crow] There it
is again, boom!

801
00:29:58,833 --> 00:30:01,300
- [Tom] Oh McRib
sandwich with McFlies.

802
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:02,833
- [Dan] There's another one!

803
00:30:02,833 --> 00:30:06,700
- [Mike] Were we supposed
to be feeding the cattle?

804
00:30:08,067 --> 00:30:09,333
- [Crow] Well Bessie'd
been depressed,

805
00:30:09,333 --> 00:30:11,767
but I didn't think
she'd do this.

806
00:30:11,767 --> 00:30:14,367
- [Tom] C'mon moo, moo damn it!

807
00:30:16,867 --> 00:30:18,133
- [Dan] I can't tell
what kinda critter

808
00:30:18,133 --> 00:30:19,433
coulda done that!

809
00:30:19,433 --> 00:30:21,433
- [Mike] Cow tipping
gone horribly wrong.

810
00:30:21,433 --> 00:30:23,400
- Eight dead cows and a calf.

811
00:30:23,400 --> 00:30:26,900
You realize what this
is gonna cost us?

812
00:30:26,900 --> 00:30:29,733
- It ain't gonna
cost us nothing.

813
00:30:29,733 --> 00:30:32,800
- Nine dead animals ain't
gonna cost us nothing?

814
00:30:32,800 --> 00:30:35,000
- You're so dumb you
wouldn't know rabbit turds

815
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,433
from Rice Crispies.

816
00:30:36,433 --> 00:30:37,700
- [Crow] Snap Crackle Poop.

817
00:30:37,700 --> 00:30:39,100
- I'll butcher up the
meat as I always do

818
00:30:39,100 --> 00:30:40,933
and I'll sell it
to Dutch's Cafe.

819
00:30:40,933 --> 00:30:42,200
- [Tom] Or to Jack in the Box.

820
00:30:42,200 --> 00:30:45,667
- You don't even know
what killed those cows!

821
00:30:45,667 --> 00:30:48,233
There might be something
horrible wrong with the meat.

822
00:30:48,233 --> 00:30:50,400
- Well that's Dutch's
lookout, not mine.

823
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:52,133
- [Mike] Brought to you
by the Pork Council.

824
00:30:52,133 --> 00:30:55,300
- [Tom] Dutch's Cafe,
on the beltline.

825
00:30:56,800 --> 00:31:00,700
- I've never seen so much
fouled up data in my life.

826
00:31:00,700 --> 00:31:02,733
It's against every
known law of physics.

827
00:31:02,733 --> 00:31:05,600
- [Mike] Except that
one that I don't know.

828
00:31:05,600 --> 00:31:07,867
- Well, we've tried
to brainstorm it.

829
00:31:07,867 --> 00:31:10,233
- [Mike] We've tried
scrubbing it out.

830
00:31:10,233 --> 00:31:11,800
- No, it just won't brainstorm.

831
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:13,000
- Right.

832
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:16,133
♪ Take your pantsuit
from your back

833
00:31:16,133 --> 00:31:17,367
- What are we gonna do?

834
00:31:17,367 --> 00:31:19,600
- [Crow] Ghostbusters!

835
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:22,033
- [Mike] Let's go down to
Dutch's for some meatloaf.

836
00:31:22,033 --> 00:31:25,767
- Doctor, do you have
a Geiger counter?

837
00:31:25,767 --> 00:31:27,600
- Yeah, in the other office.

838
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:29,267
- Good.
- Well whoopee for you.

839
00:31:29,267 --> 00:31:32,267
- Let's see if your local
sheriff will support us.

840
00:31:32,267 --> 00:31:34,200
- Sheriff Jones (laughs)?

841
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:35,867
Our Jolly Red Giant?

842
00:31:37,033 --> 00:31:39,033
I know just where
he is, let's go.

843
00:31:39,033 --> 00:31:40,467
- [Crow] Anyway,
Sixth Hour Bio Lab's

844
00:31:40,467 --> 00:31:42,800
about to start,
they need the room.

845
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:45,067
- You're gonna love him.

846
00:31:45,067 --> 00:31:47,733
You know he believes
in (mumbles) theory.

847
00:31:47,733 --> 00:31:49,967
That the moon came out
of the Pacific Ocean.

848
00:31:49,967 --> 00:31:50,800
- So do I.

849
00:31:52,267 --> 00:31:54,700
- [Mike] Y'know I don't look
at that table that often,

850
00:31:54,700 --> 00:31:58,867
just occasionally, really
it's kind of a periodic table.

851
00:32:02,233 --> 00:32:04,167
- [Crow] I love
summer in Wisconsin,

852
00:32:04,167 --> 00:32:06,400
meat rotting in the fields.

853
00:32:08,867 --> 00:32:10,267
- [Mike] The hills are alive

854
00:32:10,267 --> 00:32:12,300
with the stink of that guy,

855
00:32:12,300 --> 00:32:14,667
his back brace is smelly.

856
00:32:14,667 --> 00:32:16,967
- [Ev] Dutch is gonna
want that much meat.

857
00:32:16,967 --> 00:32:18,167
- [Dan] SO I'll
freeze some of it up

858
00:32:18,167 --> 00:32:19,667
and sell it to him later.

859
00:32:19,667 --> 00:32:22,667
- [Tom] Honey, I
don't feel fresh.

860
00:32:22,667 --> 00:32:23,833
- Hey look at this.

861
00:32:23,833 --> 00:32:25,767
- [Crow] I could
distill it and drink it!

862
00:32:25,767 --> 00:32:27,867
- I've never seen a rock
like that around here.

863
00:32:27,867 --> 00:32:28,833
- [Mike] Y'know this
movie tested well

864
00:32:28,833 --> 00:32:30,133
with sexual predators.

865
00:32:30,133 --> 00:32:32,633
- [Tom] Maybe it's breadfruit!

866
00:32:35,467 --> 00:32:37,900
- [Crow] Honey, let's play
William Burroughs and Joan.

867
00:32:37,900 --> 00:32:42,067
- [Mike] These two have every
Married with Children on tape.

868
00:32:44,567 --> 00:32:46,700
- [Tom] Well maybe we
never planted corn.

869
00:32:46,700 --> 00:32:49,133
- Wow, look at that.

870
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:51,933
I told you something
landed here last night.

871
00:32:51,933 --> 00:32:55,433
- [Crow] There's a 747
just sitting there!

872
00:32:57,067 --> 00:32:59,033
- [Mike] We've got
giant prairie dogs!

873
00:32:59,033 --> 00:33:00,900
- [Tom] Mork of Ork was
taken to St. Mary's Hospital,

874
00:33:00,900 --> 00:33:03,167
bur pronounced dead on arrival.

875
00:33:03,167 --> 00:33:05,167
- [Dan] I don't know, you
can't tell from the outside.

876
00:33:05,167 --> 00:33:06,133
- [Crow] I better climb in one

877
00:33:06,133 --> 00:33:07,733
and see what it is.

878
00:33:08,900 --> 00:33:12,100
- [Mike] Maybe their
round arrow heads.

879
00:33:12,100 --> 00:33:14,500
- [Tom] I'll juggle my
way back to his heart.

880
00:33:14,500 --> 00:33:17,567
- [Crow] And the Giant
Spider Invasion begins now!

881
00:33:17,567 --> 00:33:19,500
- [Tom] And now, begin.

882
00:33:20,433 --> 00:33:23,533
(bright synth music)

883
00:33:41,733 --> 00:33:44,233
- And good morning to you all!

884
00:33:45,400 --> 00:33:47,167
Hey Helga, you're
looking bright-eyed

885
00:33:47,167 --> 00:33:48,700
and bushy-tailed!

886
00:33:48,700 --> 00:33:50,533
You musta had some kind of a
heavy date last night, huh?

887
00:33:50,533 --> 00:33:51,667
- You better believe it.

888
00:33:51,667 --> 00:33:52,733
- One of the loggers?

889
00:33:52,733 --> 00:33:54,167
- That's my secret.

890
00:33:54,167 --> 00:33:56,367
- [Mike] What a
delightful pig I am.

891
00:33:56,367 --> 00:33:58,633
- Ah Dutch, you've got
that Linberger cheese

892
00:33:58,633 --> 00:34:00,867
smile on your face
again this morning.

893
00:34:00,867 --> 00:34:01,967
Had trouble last night?

894
00:34:01,967 --> 00:34:03,067
- Yeah.

895
00:34:03,067 --> 00:34:04,333
- One of the loggers?

896
00:34:04,333 --> 00:34:05,633
- What does that mean?

897
00:34:05,633 --> 00:34:07,867
- I don't know, I
had trouble myself!

898
00:34:07,867 --> 00:34:08,967
- [Mike] Just random words.

899
00:34:08,967 --> 00:34:10,500
- Seemed like everybody
was calling up

900
00:34:10,500 --> 00:34:11,833
with some cockamamie
little thing.

901
00:34:11,833 --> 00:34:13,000
The car wouldn't start,

902
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:14,500
the radio wouldn't work,

903
00:34:14,500 --> 00:34:16,933
and the preacher man kept
everybody awake last night!

904
00:34:16,933 --> 00:34:18,800
- When does that
gospel wonga go on?

905
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:20,233
- I don't know,
but I'll tell ya,

906
00:34:20,233 --> 00:34:21,433
he may work for God,

907
00:34:21,433 --> 00:34:23,700
but he sure hollers
like the Devil (laughs).

908
00:34:23,700 --> 00:34:25,200
- [Crow] Oh Alan!

909
00:34:25,200 --> 00:34:26,900
- [Mike] I gotta go
drain the little buddy,

910
00:34:26,900 --> 00:34:29,167
I'll be right back.

911
00:34:29,167 --> 00:34:30,433
- Breakfast is ready.

912
00:34:30,433 --> 00:34:31,467
- [Tom] Here's
your steak and eggs

913
00:34:31,467 --> 00:34:33,133
with deep-fried butter.

914
00:34:33,133 --> 00:34:36,167
- [Crow] Welcome to Hooters.

915
00:34:36,167 --> 00:34:38,967
- [Mike] Well my
thumb's clean off now.

916
00:34:38,967 --> 00:34:40,467
- No, it's not gonna work,

917
00:34:40,467 --> 00:34:42,067
go get me a hammer.

918
00:34:42,067 --> 00:34:44,300
- [Tom] No wonder
I was constipated.

919
00:34:44,300 --> 00:34:48,633
- [Crow] These are not a
lovely bunch of coconuts.

920
00:34:48,633 --> 00:34:50,800
- [Mike] We're out of gin.

921
00:34:51,833 --> 00:34:54,267
- Not that one, the big one.

922
00:34:54,267 --> 00:34:55,600
- [Tom] Stanley!

923
00:34:56,533 --> 00:34:57,967
- And a chisel.

924
00:34:57,967 --> 00:34:58,867
- [Crow] I don't
care what you use,

925
00:34:58,867 --> 00:35:00,867
just hit the guy!

926
00:35:00,867 --> 00:35:04,933
- [Mike] It's the lead
singer of the Spin Doctors.

927
00:35:04,933 --> 00:35:06,467
- [Crow] Here's
your liver honey,

928
00:35:06,467 --> 00:35:07,633
I packed it nice.

929
00:35:07,633 --> 00:35:09,133
- Get it yourself.

930
00:35:12,867 --> 00:35:15,433
- [Mike] I'm glad
he's not a Moyle.

931
00:35:15,433 --> 00:35:17,533
- [Tom] Honey MIT called.

932
00:35:20,700 --> 00:35:23,367
(monkey grunts)

933
00:35:27,767 --> 00:35:29,467
- [Crow] Man this
floor is disgusting.

934
00:35:29,467 --> 00:35:31,233
- You never were any
good with a tool.

935
00:35:31,233 --> 00:35:32,467
- [Mike] Ah, the Ropers.

936
00:35:32,467 --> 00:35:34,400
- Hey look!
- My toenail finally fell off.

937
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:35,300
- It split.

938
00:35:36,833 --> 00:35:38,500
- [Crow] Let me see.

939
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:41,867
- They look like diamonds.

940
00:35:41,867 --> 00:35:44,267
- I don't know.
- Let's get Mikey to try it.

941
00:35:44,267 --> 00:35:46,000
- May not be hard
enough to be a diamond.

942
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:47,167
- Don't hit it, no no,

943
00:35:47,167 --> 00:35:48,833
diamonds are supposed
to cut glass.

944
00:35:48,833 --> 00:35:49,833
- [Crow] They're supposed to,

945
00:35:49,833 --> 00:35:51,467
but they're too damn lazy.

946
00:35:51,467 --> 00:35:52,733
- [Mike] You see
he remembers that

947
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:55,067
from his last year of
school in third grade.

948
00:35:55,067 --> 00:35:56,167
- [Tom] Too bad their windows

949
00:35:56,167 --> 00:35:59,033
are made from cellophane
and duct tape.

950
00:35:59,033 --> 00:36:01,367
- [Crow] Aryan Nation rules.

951
00:36:04,533 --> 00:36:06,267
- Look at that!

952
00:36:06,267 --> 00:36:08,633
- [Mike] I made a R!

953
00:36:08,633 --> 00:36:11,333
(Tom hums)

954
00:36:11,333 --> 00:36:13,067
- Oh hi Dr. Langer!

955
00:36:13,067 --> 00:36:15,233
How are you this morning,
won't you join me please?

956
00:36:15,233 --> 00:36:18,567
- [Crow] Round of
bacon, I'm buying.

957
00:36:18,567 --> 00:36:20,667
- This your brother
from Oshgosh?

958
00:36:20,667 --> 00:36:22,800
- No, this is Dr.
Vance from NASA.

959
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:24,267
- [Vance] Hello sheriff.

960
00:36:24,267 --> 00:36:25,733
- NASA?

961
00:36:25,733 --> 00:36:27,733
National Aeronautics and Space
Administration, that NASA?

962
00:36:27,733 --> 00:36:30,733
- Yes, but it's
NASA, Houston Texas.

963
00:36:32,900 --> 00:36:34,600
- Sheriff, we have
to talk to you

964
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:36,733
about last night's disturbances.

965
00:36:36,733 --> 00:36:38,367
- Say no more, I'll
get that preacher man

966
00:36:38,367 --> 00:36:39,867
to tone it down tonight.

967
00:36:39,867 --> 00:36:42,433
- No no, I don't mean
that disturbance.

968
00:36:42,433 --> 00:36:43,933
- Oh no?

969
00:36:43,933 --> 00:36:45,567
Pardon me, Doctor.

970
00:36:45,567 --> 00:36:47,200
- [Tom] There's a crumb
I didn't eat there.

971
00:36:47,200 --> 00:36:48,767
- One of our local
spiders (laughs).

972
00:36:48,767 --> 00:36:51,100
- [Crow] So it's stupid
and smells of beer sweat?

973
00:36:51,100 --> 00:36:53,100
- Hey, what's that gizmo?

974
00:36:53,100 --> 00:36:54,333
- [Tom] It's my pacemaker.

975
00:36:54,333 --> 00:36:55,700
- [Vance] It's a Geiger counter.

976
00:36:55,700 --> 00:36:57,700
- A Geiger counter?

977
00:36:57,700 --> 00:36:59,833
Well we don't have any
Geigers around here,

978
00:36:59,833 --> 00:37:02,100
never did in these parts!

979
00:37:02,100 --> 00:37:03,600
- [Mike] Kill him!

980
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:07,133
- See Dr. Geiger invented this

981
00:37:07,133 --> 00:37:08,333
to count the nuclear--

982
00:37:08,333 --> 00:37:09,767
- Oh Vance, Vance,

983
00:37:09,767 --> 00:37:11,100
I have a feeling the
sheriff's putting you on.

984
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:12,933
I'm sure he's taken physics.

985
00:37:12,933 --> 00:37:16,400
- Oh I used to take physics,
but now I find that--

986
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,833
- [Crow] Joke coming in!

987
00:37:17,833 --> 00:37:19,567
- Prunes do the
better job for me!

988
00:37:19,567 --> 00:37:22,400
(audience groans)

989
00:37:23,533 --> 00:37:25,333
- We're gonna be rich!

990
00:37:25,333 --> 00:37:26,633
- Whaddya mean we?

991
00:37:26,633 --> 00:37:27,900
- [Tom] You, me and booze!

992
00:37:27,900 --> 00:37:29,500
- This farm is mine.

993
00:37:29,500 --> 00:37:32,200
Everything that's on it is mine.

994
00:37:32,200 --> 00:37:34,233
- [Mike] Every dead cow.

995
00:37:34,233 --> 00:37:35,667
- Nobody ever found diamonds

996
00:37:35,667 --> 00:37:37,467
around here before.

997
00:37:37,467 --> 00:37:38,667
I think they came out

998
00:37:38,667 --> 00:37:40,033
of that weird fireball
thing last night.

999
00:37:40,033 --> 00:37:42,133
(Mike farts)

1000
00:37:42,133 --> 00:37:43,067
- I'll take this into cousin
Billy at the rock shop.

1001
00:37:43,067 --> 00:37:44,500
- [Tom] Billy!

1002
00:37:44,500 --> 00:37:47,100
- He can tell me just
exactly what they're worth.

1003
00:37:47,100 --> 00:37:49,900
- But don't you tell cousin
Billy where you found 'em.

1004
00:37:49,900 --> 00:37:51,233
That'll be our secret.

1005
00:37:51,233 --> 00:37:53,033
- [Tom] Al Vinyl,
honey I love you!

1006
00:37:53,033 --> 00:37:54,833
- Don't look at
me like that Dan,

1007
00:37:54,833 --> 00:37:56,267
you and me are gonna be rich!

1008
00:37:56,267 --> 00:37:58,333
- [Mike] Think of the
toilet you can buy!

1009
00:37:58,333 --> 00:38:00,667
- Dan listen, I never meant
any of those nasty things

1010
00:38:00,667 --> 00:38:04,633
I used to say to you,
I was just teasing.

1011
00:38:04,633 --> 00:38:06,433
- [Crow] I'm gonna
call off the invasion,

1012
00:38:06,433 --> 00:38:09,100
this place is just not worth it.

1013
00:38:11,733 --> 00:38:14,933
- [Tom] It's them welfare
moms sucking us dry.

1014
00:38:14,933 --> 00:38:16,433
- [Dave] Hi Dr. Langer,
morning sheriff.

1015
00:38:16,433 --> 00:38:17,667
- Morning.
- Hello dear.

1016
00:38:17,667 --> 00:38:18,800
- May I join you?
- Please.

1017
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:19,667
- Thank you.

1018
00:38:19,667 --> 00:38:20,900
- This is Dave Perkins,

1019
00:38:20,900 --> 00:38:22,500
his father runs a
local newspaper.

1020
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:23,733
- [Crow] He's Mrs. Pynchon.

1021
00:38:23,733 --> 00:38:24,833
- Nice to see you.
- Nice to meet you.

1022
00:38:24,833 --> 00:38:25,867
- Dr. Vance from NASA.

1023
00:38:25,867 --> 00:38:27,133
- NASA huh?

1024
00:38:27,133 --> 00:38:28,933
- NASA, Houston.

1025
00:38:28,933 --> 00:38:30,200
- [Mike] Where they
have a problem.

1026
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:31,333
- What brings you here?

1027
00:38:31,333 --> 00:38:32,300
Anything I can
publish in the paper?

1028
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:34,433
- Well that's classified.

1029
00:38:34,433 --> 00:38:36,433
- Well, I'll put it in
the classified section.

1030
00:38:36,433 --> 00:38:37,767
- (laughs) Well
that's safe enough,

1031
00:38:37,767 --> 00:38:39,467
nobody read your ads anyway!

1032
00:38:39,467 --> 00:38:40,900
- [Tom] What a fun sheriff.

1033
00:38:40,900 --> 00:38:43,867
- Now Dave, could I speak
to you for a moment.

1034
00:38:43,867 --> 00:38:44,800
- [Dave] Sure Dr. Vance.

1035
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:46,267
- [Crow] But no touching.

1036
00:38:46,267 --> 00:38:47,867
- [Vance] Excuse
us for a moment.

1037
00:38:47,867 --> 00:38:49,833
- [Mike] Now do you recommend
the chicken fried steak

1038
00:38:49,833 --> 00:38:51,667
or the walleye cheeks?

1039
00:38:53,267 --> 00:38:55,167
- [Crow] Pudding!

1040
00:38:55,167 --> 00:38:57,300
- [Mike] Yeah you
can borrow my shirt.

1041
00:38:57,300 --> 00:38:58,600
- Is he always that serious?

1042
00:38:58,600 --> 00:38:59,767
- He probably has
something to be serious

1043
00:38:59,767 --> 00:39:01,433
about this time.

1044
00:39:01,433 --> 00:39:02,967
- You know I wonder
if what happened

1045
00:39:02,967 --> 00:39:04,500
to Terry and I last
night has something

1046
00:39:04,500 --> 00:39:06,533
to do with what
you're talking about.

1047
00:39:06,533 --> 00:39:07,400
- What?
- What happened

1048
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:08,533
to you and Terry?

1049
00:39:08,533 --> 00:39:09,433
- [Tom] First base, whew!

1050
00:39:09,433 --> 00:39:10,900
- By the junk yard,

1051
00:39:10,900 --> 00:39:13,100
the lights, they went dead,
the radio wouldn't work

1052
00:39:13,100 --> 00:39:14,867
and the engine wouldn't start.

1053
00:39:14,867 --> 00:39:16,300
The wind came up and
started, I don't know,

1054
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:18,567
everything just went wrong.

1055
00:39:18,567 --> 00:39:20,200
- [Tom] Thoughtful or
hungry, you decide.

1056
00:39:20,200 --> 00:39:22,133
- [Mike] Hour three
of the invasion,

1057
00:39:22,133 --> 00:39:24,500
we took the refrigerator.

1058
00:39:24,500 --> 00:39:25,433
- [Crow] Thanks for
breakfast ma'am,

1059
00:39:25,433 --> 00:39:26,600
I'll clean up.

1060
00:39:28,733 --> 00:39:30,000
- [Mike] Doctor should
have been more specific

1061
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:33,400
when he told her to
get plenty of fluids.

1062
00:39:37,767 --> 00:39:39,767
Honey I need changing again.

1063
00:39:39,767 --> 00:39:42,433
- You're hitting the
booze again, huh?

1064
00:39:42,433 --> 00:39:44,533
- Leave me alone,
I feel terrible.

1065
00:39:44,533 --> 00:39:47,033
This place is full of spiders.

1066
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,433
- Yeah, I know.

1067
00:39:49,433 --> 00:39:51,200
Little pink ones.

1068
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:53,967
- No no, big, big
black hairy ones,

1069
00:39:53,967 --> 00:39:55,100
with furry legs.

1070
00:39:55,100 --> 00:39:56,300
- [Crow] No that's me.

1071
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:59,833
- Lay off the booze,
Ev and they'll go away.

1072
00:39:59,833 --> 00:40:01,300
- [Mike] Y'know in her defense,

1073
00:40:01,300 --> 00:40:03,667
laying off the booze would
mean seeing him sober.

1074
00:40:03,667 --> 00:40:05,400
- [Crow] It's true.

1075
00:40:05,400 --> 00:40:07,867
(phone rings)

1076
00:40:07,867 --> 00:40:10,167
- [Mike] Joey Hasbeen.

1077
00:40:10,167 --> 00:40:12,433
- Hello, Sheriff's office?

1078
00:40:12,433 --> 00:40:14,167
Oh yes Mrs. Cooper, how are you?

1079
00:40:14,167 --> 00:40:16,900
- [Tom] Pancakes,
I'll be right over!

1080
00:40:16,900 --> 00:40:18,833
- Missing?
- Well where are you?

1081
00:40:18,833 --> 00:40:20,033
Well take a good look around

1082
00:40:20,033 --> 00:40:21,233
and that's where you would be.

1083
00:40:21,233 --> 00:40:22,367
- Where'd you see him last?

1084
00:40:22,367 --> 00:40:24,067
- [Mike] 1953?

1085
00:40:24,067 --> 00:40:26,533
- You haven't seen
him since last night?

1086
00:40:26,533 --> 00:40:28,433
Well I'd be glad to drive out

1087
00:40:28,433 --> 00:40:29,600
and take a look for him,

1088
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:31,200
what color is his motorcycle?

1089
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:32,133
- [Tom] Personally
I've never been able

1090
00:40:32,133 --> 00:40:33,600
to start seeing motorcycles.

1091
00:40:33,600 --> 00:40:35,100
- C'mon dear, please
stop worrying,

1092
00:40:35,100 --> 00:40:37,000
I'm sure he'll turn
up safe and sound.

1093
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:39,200
- [Crow] I'll be there
after my pre-lunch snack.

1094
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:41,100
- Yes, I'll get
in touch with you.

1095
00:40:41,100 --> 00:40:42,000
Right, bye.

1096
00:40:44,500 --> 00:40:47,567
(bright synth music)

1097
00:40:53,733 --> 00:40:55,733
- Boy, how come
you only get tired

1098
00:40:55,733 --> 00:40:57,300
when you have to stay awake

1099
00:40:57,300 --> 00:41:01,267
to avoid being replaced by an
evil pod creature, huh Servo?

1100
00:41:01,267 --> 00:41:03,200
Servo!
- I'm awake Mike,

1101
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:06,667
I can stay awake, I just
need a little shut eye.

1102
00:41:06,667 --> 00:41:08,833
- No no no no, don't
pass out on me now,

1103
00:41:08,833 --> 00:41:11,267
we have to stay awake
to avoid being replaced

1104
00:41:11,267 --> 00:41:15,133
by a pod creature from
Gypsy's evil doppleganger.

1105
00:41:15,133 --> 00:41:17,433
- Please Mike, (speaks German).

1106
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:20,433
(Both speak German)

1107
00:41:22,133 --> 00:41:24,700
- Round your lips.
- I'll round your lips.

1108
00:41:24,700 --> 00:41:26,233
Crow!
- I'm fine, I'm fine,

1109
00:41:26,233 --> 00:41:29,267
Mike I have French roast,
Vivaren, diet pills,

1110
00:41:29,267 --> 00:41:33,033
Mountain Dew, Jolt,
water Joe, Surge,

1111
00:41:33,033 --> 00:41:35,700
chocolate covered
espresso beans, M&M's,

1112
00:41:35,700 --> 00:41:36,933
and I'm listening to (mumbles)

1113
00:41:36,933 --> 00:41:39,267
and I'm fine Mike,
really I'm fine.

1114
00:41:39,267 --> 00:41:41,733
- Alright okay,
just don't explode.

1115
00:41:41,733 --> 00:41:42,567
- Okay, Roger.
- I'm gonna check in

1116
00:41:42,567 --> 00:41:44,167
on the planet here.

1117
00:41:45,633 --> 00:41:49,633
- Hi Nelson, just getting
the last of these ticks off.

1118
00:41:50,533 --> 00:41:52,600
- Bobo, is that you?

1119
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:54,100
I mean really you?

1120
00:41:55,300 --> 00:41:57,200
- No it's John Shuck
on a bad hair day,

1121
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:59,567
of course it's me, and I'm fine.

1122
00:41:59,567 --> 00:42:01,533
But these two (laughs),

1123
00:42:01,533 --> 00:42:03,267
they really love
their zucchinis!

1124
00:42:03,267 --> 00:42:04,800
In fact, they're packing them up

1125
00:42:04,800 --> 00:42:06,567
so that they can deliver
zucchinis to their friends

1126
00:42:06,567 --> 00:42:08,233
all over the galaxy!

1127
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:11,667
- Now listen very
carefully Bobo,

1128
00:42:11,667 --> 00:42:13,267
those pods grow aliens

1129
00:42:13,267 --> 00:42:14,533
that replace your body,

1130
00:42:14,533 --> 00:42:16,100
if they're loading
them into the truck,

1131
00:42:16,100 --> 00:42:19,267
that means the whole
galaxy could be in danger!

1132
00:42:19,267 --> 00:42:22,500
- Oh come now, just
because they load

1133
00:42:22,500 --> 00:42:24,167
a bunch of zucchini
throw pillows

1134
00:42:24,167 --> 00:42:25,633
onto a truck, doesn't mean

1135
00:42:25,633 --> 00:42:27,733
they're trying to
take over the galaxy.

1136
00:42:27,733 --> 00:42:30,233
(laughs) Preposterous,
typical of you

1137
00:42:30,233 --> 00:42:33,667
with your Beck and your
bra and hand blenders.

1138
00:42:33,667 --> 00:42:35,133
Well look, I'll just ask her.

1139
00:42:35,133 --> 00:42:38,667
Oh hey Law Giver, now
are those evil pods

1140
00:42:38,667 --> 00:42:42,000
and are you trying to
take over the galaxy?

1141
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:44,667
- Yes and yes, excuse me please.

1142
00:42:48,133 --> 00:42:50,200
- Well I guess I can see

1143
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:52,000
how you could
misconstrue that Nelson,

1144
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:53,700
but I'm still not convinced.

1145
00:42:53,700 --> 00:42:55,000
- What do you mean?

1146
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:58,333
Calm down, look
just do me a favor

1147
00:42:58,333 --> 00:43:01,367
and try taking one of
those pods off the truck.

1148
00:43:01,367 --> 00:43:03,533
- Alright, I'll humor you.

1149
00:43:04,967 --> 00:43:08,233
Let me see if I can grab
one of these babies here.

1150
00:43:08,233 --> 00:43:09,233
There we go.

1151
00:43:13,567 --> 00:43:17,733
Hmm, I don't remember taking
another one of those with me.

1152
00:43:20,500 --> 00:43:23,133
Well now, this is odd,

1153
00:43:23,133 --> 00:43:26,400
and she did say she wanted
to take over the galazy.

1154
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:29,300
(Pearl screams)

1155
00:43:29,300 --> 00:43:31,100
Nelson I see your point,

1156
00:43:31,100 --> 00:43:32,633
you may be onto something!

1157
00:43:32,633 --> 00:43:34,600
The universe is in danger,

1158
00:43:34,600 --> 00:43:37,000
but don't you worry,
no sirree Bob,

1159
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:38,567
I'm on the job!

1160
00:43:38,567 --> 00:43:40,233
I'll stop these two
wretched creatures

1161
00:43:40,233 --> 00:43:41,833
and foil their little plan.

1162
00:43:41,833 --> 00:43:45,600
(Bobo's speech is
muffled by rope)

1163
00:43:45,600 --> 00:43:47,833
- Well again, we're doomed.

1164
00:43:49,533 --> 00:43:50,767
- What's that horrible thumping?

1165
00:43:50,767 --> 00:43:52,233
- It's my heart.

1166
00:43:52,233 --> 00:43:54,800
I think I'm--
- He's gonna blow!

1167
00:43:56,100 --> 00:43:58,667
(alarms blare)

1168
00:44:10,767 --> 00:44:14,500
- [Crow] Hurry up, hurry
up you guys, please!

1169
00:44:15,667 --> 00:44:18,533
- [Mike] The last
(mumbles), wee-hee!

1170
00:44:18,533 --> 00:44:19,600
- [Tom] I'm gonna
pre-bury myself

1171
00:44:19,600 --> 00:44:21,700
to save time after I die.

1172
00:44:25,933 --> 00:44:29,267
- [Crow] He's a
freelance pooper scooper!

1173
00:44:29,267 --> 00:44:33,000
- [Mike] They whacked
the Cryptkeeper!

1174
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:36,200
- [Crow] Whatever it is, it's
drizzled with chocolate sauce!

1175
00:44:36,200 --> 00:44:38,300
- [Mike] Honey, you up?

1176
00:44:38,300 --> 00:44:42,233
- [Tom] George Hamilton
finally over-tans.

1177
00:44:42,233 --> 00:44:44,567
- [Crow] Death of
a kabuki actor.

1178
00:44:44,567 --> 00:44:47,067
(heart beats)

1179
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:52,167
- [Tom] Does the
coroner need to know?

1180
00:44:53,700 --> 00:44:55,433
- [Crow] I'd like
to say a few words,

1181
00:44:55,433 --> 00:44:58,433
this guy's dead,
the end, thank you.

1182
00:44:59,700 --> 00:45:01,367
- [Mike] Well happy Arbor Day.

1183
00:45:01,367 --> 00:45:02,400
- [Crow] What was that
waiter's name in Paris?

1184
00:45:02,400 --> 00:45:03,233
Jean Luc!

1185
00:45:07,367 --> 00:45:08,767
- [Mike] Hey Gary,
does this strike you

1186
00:45:08,767 --> 00:45:12,100
as a really gross
planet we're invading?

1187
00:45:15,100 --> 00:45:18,167
- [Crow] Wait, what
am I doing, Jeez!

1188
00:45:19,933 --> 00:45:23,300
- You okay?
- I'm coming down, thanks!

1189
00:45:23,300 --> 00:45:24,333
- [Mike] What, do they
keep their garbage

1190
00:45:24,333 --> 00:45:25,700
in the refrigerator?

1191
00:45:25,700 --> 00:45:29,267
- [Tom] An afternoon
with Sandra Loch!

1192
00:45:29,267 --> 00:45:31,067
- [Crow] I'm not looking,
repeat not looking

1193
00:45:31,067 --> 00:45:33,100
at the contents of the blender.

1194
00:45:33,100 --> 00:45:34,367
- [Mike] These people
are really the backbone

1195
00:45:34,367 --> 00:45:36,633
of your casino-based economy.

1196
00:45:36,633 --> 00:45:37,900
- What's the matter with you?

1197
00:45:37,900 --> 00:45:38,700
- [Crow] Just caught
a glimpse of myself

1198
00:45:38,700 --> 00:45:40,433
in the hallway mirror.

1199
00:45:43,167 --> 00:45:44,100
- [Mike] Well if I
know that spider,

1200
00:45:44,100 --> 00:45:46,700
it's not a virgin bloody Mary!

1201
00:45:46,700 --> 00:45:47,767
- [Tom] Whee!

1202
00:45:49,633 --> 00:45:53,633
- [Crow] We still on of the
Richard Feinmen lecture?

1203
00:45:53,633 --> 00:45:55,333
- You look like you
could use a drink.

1204
00:45:55,333 --> 00:45:58,433
- [Tom] And a shower and a job.

1205
00:45:58,433 --> 00:46:00,367
- I found another body.

1206
00:46:00,367 --> 00:46:01,667
- [Mike] Good, yours is
getting pretty gross.

1207
00:46:01,667 --> 00:46:03,667
- Another cow?

1208
00:46:03,667 --> 00:46:05,400
- No, a human body.

1209
00:46:05,400 --> 00:46:08,033
- [Crow] It was walking along
the street and I killed it.

1210
00:46:08,033 --> 00:46:09,267
- A person?

1211
00:46:09,267 --> 00:46:12,167
- [Tom] Dutch will only
give me $0.39 a pound.

1212
00:46:12,167 --> 00:46:15,767
- But it was chewed up
worse than them cow.

1213
00:46:17,167 --> 00:46:19,000
- [Mike] Funny, I used
to like things like that.

1214
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:20,333
- We need to call the sheriff.

1215
00:46:20,333 --> 00:46:22,600
- Are you out of your mind?

1216
00:46:22,600 --> 00:46:26,367
Now I buried that body,
and I hid the motorcycle,

1217
00:46:26,367 --> 00:46:28,033
no one will ever know.

1218
00:46:28,033 --> 00:46:29,533
- You're crazy!

1219
00:46:29,533 --> 00:46:32,133
- We can't let that sheriff
come nosing around here!

1220
00:46:32,133 --> 00:46:34,733
What if he finds the diamonds?

1221
00:46:34,733 --> 00:46:37,033
And all that grass
we're growing?

1222
00:46:37,033 --> 00:46:38,700
- [Tom] Wands are
illegal in Wisconsin?

1223
00:46:38,700 --> 00:46:39,567
- Well you sound like
you've been smoking

1224
00:46:39,567 --> 00:46:41,133
the stuff yourself.

1225
00:46:42,233 --> 00:46:45,067
- [Crow] Oh, my
bloody Mary has legs!

1226
00:46:50,867 --> 00:46:55,433
- [Mike] Charlotte's doing
bachelor parties now!

1227
00:46:55,433 --> 00:46:56,800
- [Crow] Wow, the
family on Tobacco Road

1228
00:46:56,800 --> 00:46:59,567
had a nicer farm than this.

1229
00:46:59,567 --> 00:47:02,933
- [Mike] Hey pal, you
got any curds and whey?

1230
00:47:02,933 --> 00:47:07,067
- [Tom] He's doing kind
of a grunge Amish look.

1231
00:47:07,067 --> 00:47:08,900
- [Crow] My assignment,
take out the greasy hick

1232
00:47:08,900 --> 00:47:11,167
with extreme prejudice.

1233
00:47:11,167 --> 00:47:14,433
- [Mike] I'm proud
to be a crap farmer.

1234
00:47:15,800 --> 00:47:18,067
- [Tom] Please sir, you're
standing on my wife.

1235
00:47:18,067 --> 00:47:20,000
- [Crow] Shine, mister?

1236
00:47:22,067 --> 00:47:25,400
(bird squawks)
- Why is he cawing?

1237
00:47:25,400 --> 00:47:29,400
- [Tom] I attempted the north
face of Mount Cheesehead.

1238
00:47:29,400 --> 00:47:33,200
- [Crow] Sheesh,
Mr. Touchy wigs out.

1239
00:47:33,200 --> 00:47:34,867
Hoo, hah, missed me!

1240
00:47:37,267 --> 00:47:38,800
- That creepeth upon the Earth

1241
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:40,767
shall be an abomination.

1242
00:47:40,767 --> 00:47:42,300
- [Tom] Gotta nip it in the bud!

1243
00:47:42,300 --> 00:47:46,367
- [Preacher] Only the pure
of heart shall be spared.

1244
00:47:46,367 --> 00:47:50,700
- [Crow] Oh, spider's
barbecue got outta control.

1245
00:47:50,700 --> 00:47:53,167
- Ah, it's you.
- Don Juan DeStinko.

1246
00:47:53,167 --> 00:47:54,500
- I told ya I could
come again tonight.

1247
00:47:54,500 --> 00:47:55,433
- No!
- No!

1248
00:47:55,433 --> 00:47:57,433
- How'd you swing it, honey?

1249
